{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"injurious-wellmade-moth","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"# S1 — Isolate review-gate scratch on a dedicated EBS volume\n\n## Plan\nAdd the structural Option C fix: a dedicated gp3 EBS volume for code-review gate scratch, mounted at a documented host path (for example `/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch`) and wired so review snapshots and clone tempdirs use that filesystem instead of root. Reuse the existing EBS attach/mount pattern from `infra/terraform/user_data.sh:20-70`: pass the volume id through Terraform `templatefile`, resolve Nitro NVMe by volume id, format idempotently, mount by UUID in `/etc/fstab`.\n\nConfigure the review-bot container so `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` points at the mounted scratch path. Because `src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py:381` uses `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"reviewbot-\")` and low-disk admission checks `tempfile.gettempdir()` (`src/rebar/review_bot/low_disk.py:69`), also set container tempdir (`TMPDIR` or equivalent) so both `reviewbot-*` clone workdirs and `rebar-gate-snapshots` leave root. Preserve the existing snapshot janitor semantics; this story moves the filesystem, it does not redesign the cache.\n\nAdd a dedicated CloudWatch alarm for the scratch volume's usage/cap. Extend `infra/scripts/observability.sh` to publish a mount-specific metric for the scratch mount (same style as `/var/gerrit` at `observability.sh:72-78`) and add Terraform alarm wiring. Document provisioning and recovery in runbooks.\n\n## Grounding\n- Current data-volume Terraform: `infra/terraform/main.tf:27-35`, attachment at `:83-87`.\n- Current root block device: `infra/terraform/main.tf:56-59`, variable in `infra/terraform/variables.tf:13-17`.\n- Current scratch is root-resident because `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` is unset: `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:233-245`; `repo_snapshot.py:149-163`.\n- Current runbook states clone workdirs are root-volume resident: `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md:575-606`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Terraform declares a separate scratch EBS volume, attachment, size variable, outputs/tags, and lifecycle policy appropriate for replaceable scratch (unlike `/var/gerrit`, no source-of-truth data is stored there).\n- [ ] Host provisioning mounts the scratch volume idempotently by UUID and fails loud if it cannot mount.\n- [ ] Review-bot snapshot store and clone tempdirs both resolve to the scratch volume, not root.\n- [ ] Scratch volume publishes a CloudWatch metric and has its own alarm wired to SNS.\n- [ ] Runbooks document steady-state location, alarm meaning, recovery, and that scratch is rebuildable.\n- [ ] Validation includes targeted tests for Terraform alarm/action conventions, compose/env wiring, and observability metric emission.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: the control is Terraform + Linux mount/env configuration with local tests; it does not depend on a GitHub-only CI signal.","id":"aa40-cbda-ee38-481c","parent_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","priority":1,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","scratch-volume"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"S1 — Isolate review-gate scratch on a dedicated EBS volume"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788375027120785317,"uuid":"042db4c0-eb6a-4bf6-80a5-1e6c1548da49"}